  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man with a shaved head covered in shaving cream, using a razor to shave his scalp, with text overlay reading 'why don't i get sunburnt' and 'i use sunscreen'. The visual metaphor humorously suggests that the man's bald head is his 'sunscreen', implying he doesn't get sunburnt because he has no hair to absorb UV rays. The meme's intent is to make a lighthearted, self-deprecating joke about sun protection, using absurdity and visual exaggeration. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it does not target any specific group based on race, gender, religion, or other protected characteristics. The humor is derived from the illogical and exaggerated premise, not from disparaging or harmful content. The overall intent is to entertain through absurd analogical mapping: the concept of sunscreen is humorously equated with the physical absence of hair on the scalp.",
